 and operator.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Do I have to carry the permit in the vehicle?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"Yes. Section 7E requires any person operating a vehicle with authorized flashing, rotating or oscillating red lights to have the permit on their person or in the vehicle in an easily accessible place.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Can volunteer firefighters use blue lights in Massachusetts?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"No. The blue light authorization in Massachusetts is tied to law enforcement affiliation, unlike neighboring Connecticut where blue is the volunteer firefighter color.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"What is the penalty for illegal emergency lights in Massachusetts?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"Where no other penalty is provided, section 7E sets a fine of not less than one hundred dollars and not more than three hundred dollars, in addition to permit revocation.\"\n      \t}\n    \t}\n  \t]\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"Organization\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\",\n  \t\"name\": \"Strobes N' More\",\n  \t\"url\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/\",\n  \t\"telephone\": \"+1-401-454-4487\",\n  \t\"email\": \"sales@strobesnmore.com\",\n  \t\"address\": {\n    \t\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\n    \t\"streetAddress\": \"81 Tom Harvey Road\",\n    \t\"addressLocality\": \"Westerly\",\n    \t\"addressRegion\": \"RI\",\n    \t\"postalCode\": \"02891\",\n    \t\"addressCountry\": \"US\"\n  \t}\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"WebSite\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#website\",\n  \t\"url\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/\",\n  \t\"name\": \"Strobes N' More\",\n  \t\"